-- title:
--   Multiplicity of the fibre centre in (c) equals ord_w(c)
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq F \subseteq F'$ be fields, with $F$ and $F'$ algebras over $K$ and $F'$ an algebra over $F$ forming a scalar tower, and assume $F'/F$ is finite and separable. Let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, that is, a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring, and let $w$ be such a place of $F'$ over $K$; assume $w$ lies over $v$ in the sense that the preimage of the valuation subring of $w$ under $F \to F'$ is exactly the valuation subring of $v$. Write `Place.integralClosureAt F' v` for the integral closure of the valuation ring of $v$ in $F'$, a Dedekind domain with fraction field $F'$, and `Place.fiberCenter F' v hw` for the height-one prime of that ring obtained as the centre of $w$, i.e. the contraction of the maximal ideal of $w$. Then for every nonzero element $c$ of this integral closure, the multiplicity of the prime ideal of `Place.fiberCenter F' v hw` in the normalised factorisation of the principal ideal generated by $c$ equals the natural number obtained by truncating $w.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $c$ in $F'$, where $\mathrm{ord}$ denotes minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation.
--
--   This is the dictionary, for a finite separable extension, between the order of vanishing of a function at a place $w$ lying over $v$ and the exponent of the corresponding prime of the integral closure of $\mathcal{O}_v$ in the factorisation of a principal ideal; summed over the places above $v$ it gives $(c) = \prod_{w \mid v} P_w^{\operatorname{ord}_w(c)}$. It is used in [`AlgebraicCurve.Place.exists_integralClosureAt_of_ord_fiber_nonneg`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Place.exists_integralClosureAt_of_ord_fiber_nonneg), and so underlies the integrality of functions without poles along a fibre.
